      "TWO holes under one high-water mark: the step-4 pull delivers the committed-and-visible seq 7 while BOTH seq 5 and seq 6 are still in-flight (pg_visible_in_snapshot, SQL:visibility-horizon), so the refined horizon encodes the composite cursor '7~5.6': high-water 7, holes 5 and 6 joined by the '.' hole separator (the opaque token, D-cursor-opaque-token; see ../../../spec/cursor-token.ts). fencing/001's single-hole token '6~5' pins no separator: only a token carrying two or more holes distinguishes a correct codec from one that joins them with another byte",
      "has_more is true: the boundary stays open while the token carries pending holes, so the client stages seq 7 invisibly and its durable checkpoint is still '4' at step 5 (no-intermediate-commit)",
      "the transport fault at step 6 was never applied (P:verdict-completeness-transforms-and-conflict-rejection), so the client re-issues the poll from its committed checkpoint '4'",
      "after both held transactions resolve, the step-7 pull delivers seq 5, seq 6 AND seq 7 and the cursor closes to the flat decimal '7': every hole is delayed, never skipped (P:keyset-pagination-and-delivery-bound)"
